Revision: f359d43b406057f1a8cdbc4ea93b827642c162e6

The files under upstream/ are unmodified copies identified in upstream.lock.json.
LICENSE and upstream/LICENSE preserve the upstream license text.

skills/modernize/SKILL.md, its references, and the Copilot command and specialist
instructions adapt the upstream entry, review, brief, transform, verification,
business-rule extraction, test-engineer and architecture-critic approaches,
modified on 2026-10-22, 2026-10-23, 2026-10-25 and 2026-11-03 for native Copilot chat, conversational
continuation, project setup discovery, adapter review and lifecycle checks,
explicit evidence limitations, and a subsequent Playwright BDD legacy
baseline with current source/test/environment evidence checks. The port preserves
upstream review/brief artifact conventions while adapting routine approvals,
questions, scoped candidate verification and client tool names to native chat.
The status guidance and optional report follow the upstream saved-artifact
overview approach. scripts/build_report.py and assets/report/report.html are new
implementations for this port's artifacts; they do not implement upstream proof verdicts.
scripts/inventory.py wraps the unmodified upstream sharder and adds file hashes,
selection identity, HTML/HTM source selection, and a read-only JSON interface.

The discovery artifact validator, native result, baseline and candidate evidence checkers,
workflow compatibility probe, tests, and documentation are additions to this port.
The unchanged workflow probe is packaged separately under
diagnostics/workflow-probe/ as an optional isolated diagnostic; the normal
modernization plugin does not load it.
This project does not imply endorsement by Anthropic, GitHub, or the Guardian.

The 0.4.0 port also adapts preflight, assessment, mapping, extraction, uplift,
reimagine and hardening, with native Copilot specialist profiles. The original
comparison, baseline, rule-tracing, uplift and proof helpers are bundled unchanged.
scripts/upstream_checks.py dispatches those helpers and adapts existing R-prefixed
rule IDs and optional prepared-source snapshots without rewriting saved records.
Claude UI hooks, telemetry and Workflow execution are not included. All unchanged
imports are identified by path and hash in upstream.lock.json.

The E2E setup and scenario-quality guidance, added on 2026-11-11, uses original
wording informed by the Guardian Agentsy E2E playbook and feature-files practices.
